{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791819240,"nonce":"eiO2Nf3o1UKLlmpWcub0FqLm2F0=","title":"Canvas.render (haxe/ashui/ui/Canvas.hx lines 180-195) always registers an AnimationScheduler ticker when the animate prop exists. The callback returns alive even when animate is false. AnimationScheduler.hasActive consequently stays true throughout the owner's lifetime and WindowedApp wakes every 50 ms while paused, even with no repaint.","message":"Reproduced through ChimpMonk editor/bin/editor.hl, whose viewport uses animate={doc.playing}. Diagnostics show document.playing=false, running=false, one remaining ticker, zero springs and no scheme animation.\n\nAfter separately guarding the editor's settled layout observers against unchanged signal writes, the editor renders only 3 startup frames and zero frames after 8 s, but still consumes 1.3% CPU over seconds 10-20. With temporary reactive ticker gating as well: 3 startup frames, no idle frames, 0.0-0.1% ps samples and 0.2% CPU-time delta (0.02 CPU seconds over 10.02 elapsed seconds).\n\nCandidate: start a single ticker when the reactive animate value becomes true, return false when paused or disposed, and restart reactively when playback resumes. Production implementation must verify false-at-creation, true/false/resume transitions, rapid toggles, owner cleanup and late frame callback updates, while preserving visibility behavior and active animation pacing.\n\nInvestigation only: no production sources changed. Full proof builds, timings, sampled stacks and measurements at .ashui/snapshots/chimpmonk-idle/. Follow the linked ChimpMonk observer-feedback issue for the original 36-40% redraw load. No push.","files":null}]}